{"duration_api_ms":870900,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d12fd3bb-9b26-4863-abef-054c3205f748","total_cost_usd":9.458969999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191930,"cache_read_input_tokens":11608676,"output_tokens":69305,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":34539},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":191930,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2663,"cache_read_input_tokens":200715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1737,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001827,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":176,"outputTokens":69305,"cacheReadInputTokens":11608676,"cacheCreationInputTokens":191930,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":9.457143,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":96,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The correction is complete and verified. Here is the candidate for independent review.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nThe worker records the provider **process's** own `ended_at` when that process exits and *then* runs its verification command. In that window the invocation duration is frozen while the stage is still open — and all three shared surfaces printed `running 15s`: a frozen figure under a live word, getting more convincing as the clock moved. Reproduced before the change on `just status`, the viewer list and the viewer detail from one document.\n\n## The change\n\n`stage_timing` now records *which* invocation it interpreted (`invocation`: `active` / `ended` / `None`) and labels the measure accordingly in one shared place (`_INVOCATION_LABELS`), so no surface composes its own wording:\n\n| case | duration line | extra line |\n|---|---|---|\n| active invocation | `running 30s` (moves with the observation clock) | — |\n| ended invocation, stage still open | `provider ran 15s` (frozen) | `provider invocation ended after 15s; this stage has not ended` |\n| ended invocation, terminal stage | `provider ran 15s` | — (state + `timeout not applicable (stage ended)` already say it) |\n| unattributed / malformed / foreign / future / stale | `running unknown` | — |\n| never started | `not started` | — |\n\n`running`/`running_seconds` stay as the bare measure; `duration` is what surfaces print. Preserved unchanged: active elapsed, terminal frozen duration, Job age, provider/stage/Job deadlines and timeout causes (an ended process still stops limiting the stage), every unknown/malformed/future/foreign-attempt/stale qualification, the 15-second freshness rule, runtime details and worker-declared failure causes. Real CLI output checked for both the ended and the live stage in one Job (`tools/job_viewer.py --status`, `tools/stack.py status`) — the two surfaces agree word for word.\n\n## Candidate\n\n- **Base:** `ac17a5add7a58fcd845a8eee7485a633ef917de3` (admitted checkpoint; task identity `fd3e8b90-W1` preserved, no handoff written)\n- **Diff digest:** `10045d7278dea070…`, 7 files, +555/−34\n- **Changed paths** (sha256, first 16): `v12/python/tools/job_observation.py` `a78bf16545cea516` · `tools/job_viewer.py` `c6021572ad130f3c` · `tools/stack.py` `d74753a983fa9494` · `JOB-VIEWER.md` `9177a14060848a54` · `tests/tools/test_job_observation.py` `2818e39e6d707471` · `tests/tools/test_job_viewer.py` `5dbca278377b161c` · `tests/manager/test_exchange.py` `cc4041ecda17e24d`\n\nNo collector, log parser, telemetry producer or scheduling-policy change; no publication optimization; no import into the host and no live instance touched.\n\n## Test evidence (all simulated-document; no live provider ran)\n\nMandatory four-module verification, exactly as supplied:\n- `env BATON_V12_STACK_TEST_ROOT=/scratch BATON_V12_DISK_ROOT=/scratch TMPDIR=/scratch PYTHONPATH=v12/python/src:v12/python python3 -m unittest -v tests.manager.test_attempt_failure_cause tests.tools.test_attempt_diagnostics tests.tools.test_job_observation tests.tools.test_job_viewer` → **300 tests, OK, 9.831s** (baseline at the admitted checkpoint: 284 tests, OK, 9.996s). No failures, no skips.\n\nNew focused coverage — 17 cases, each positive and negative:\n- `tests.tools.test_job_observation.AnEndedInvocationIsNotARunningOne` — 11 cases, 0.003s: active invocation (and that its figure *moves*), ended invocation over `running`/`reviewing`/`integrating`/`answering`, the frozen figure across three later observation clocks, ended provider deadline no longer limiting, terminal stage with and without a recorded end, ten unattributed/malformed/foreign/future spoilings, never-started, three-surface word-for-word agreement, list-column/stage-id and `!! STALE` preservation, worker-declared cause still rendered beside it.\n- `tests.tools.test_job_viewer.TheDurationSaysWhetherItIsStillRunning` — 5 cases, 0.032s: list row and detail rows over real `projection.status` documents.\n- `tests.manager.test_exchange.InvocationTiming.test_real_publisher_ended_invocation_is_not_reported_as_running` — producer-grounded: the real `baton_worker._ActivityPublisher` writes the invocation event, the real `exchange.observation` reads it back, the shared views render it (`provider ran 8s`, `stage timeout in 3m48s`). Still simulated — no provider process was launched.\n\nNeighbouring modules:\n- 9 modules incl. `tests.manager.test_exchange`, `tests.tools.test_worker_visibility`, `tests.job_manager.test_status`, `tests.manager.test_boundary_inventory` → **882 tests, OK, 194.6s**.\n- 5 modules incl. `tests.tools.test_stack` → **375 tests, 6 failures, 38.8s**. All six are in `tests/tools/test_stack.py` and **pre-existing**: the same six fail at the admitted checkpoint on a pristine extract, and the message is byte-identical (`snapshot … written -1.0s ago` → read as stale; a sandbox file-mtime/clock artifact). The pristine extract additionally showed 2 errors in `ValidIdleComposition` that do not occur in this tree — an artifact of running from a copied tree, not a delta of this change.\n\n## Remaining limitations for the reviewer\n\n1. **Deliberately not changed:** a *terminal* stage whose invocation never recorded an ending still reads `running unknown` (pre-existing wording for an absent measure, asserted in the new coverage). It states no duration and implies no outcome, so I left the unknown qualification exactly as it was rather than widening the diff; say if you want `duration unknown` there instead.\n2. `running`/`running_seconds` remain on the shared result as the bare measure. A future surface could reintroduce the defect by printing `\"running \" + one[\"running\"]`; the guard is behavioural (every surface asserted against `running\\s+15s`), not structural.\n3. The list row's duration column is 19 wide — every spelling under 100 hours fits; beyond that the later columns shift by one, as they already did.\n4. No live-provider evidence exists in this environment: the strongest link in the chain is the real worker publisher → real exchange reader → shared views.","ttft_ms":1647,"type":"result","duration_ms":1497910,"uuid":"372b5488-1699-4885-870f-bfeb0672cd50","ttft_stream_ms":1155,"time_to_request_ms":72,"queued_turn_count":0}
